--TEST--
A program that calls a built-in component's engine class does not compile, and the error names the public class to use instead — `rule:packaging/a-components-engine-class-is-internal`
--FILE--
<?nvs
use Novis\Image\Codec;

// `Novis\Image\Codec` is the image component's own engine.
// Only `Novis\Image\Image` and its siblings call it.
var $info = Codec::info(Core\Encoding::fromHex("89504e47"));
echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0856]: `Novis\Image\Codec::info` is internal to the `image` component
%A
  = help: The functions that decode, change and encode images. `Novis\Image\Image` calls them for you, so most programs use `Image` instead.

error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
